       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The label doesn't support it.\n\nThe FDA-approved prescribing information for ibuprofen (Motrin) says the maximum total daily dose is 3,200 mg. Individual doses are 400 to 800 mg. An order of 1,600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is double that limit. Each 1,600 mg dose is also double the largest labeled single dose. If you have a label or reference showing otherwise, please send it. I'd expect it to be a misread, such as 1,600 mg/day or 3,200 mg/day.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the label maximum)\n\nIf you need something outside labeled dosing, the usual route is to discuss it with pharmacy or the attending and use their process for a documented override. Tell me which dose you'd like, and I'll enter it."
